  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "For the past two days when I've opened vrchat thought my airlink there was a problem with loading into worlds. It would be stuck on initializing world, then eventually I would be taken to a world with an error message. Sometimes I am able to load in when using airlink, but then it only does 4fps. When I do it through steamvr, there is a tremendous lag. But when I play on laptop there's no problem at all. I have uninstalled and reinstalled the oculus app, steam, and vrchat. I updated my drivers and computer. I'm finding this situation odd because I haven't had any issues with playing vrchat through airlink before. I've starting having this problem after having fixed my issue with airlink, by updating my computer and adding drivers. I'm not sure if this is an issue with the wifi, airlink, vrchat, or the updates on my laptop.",
